  <h1>Site Information</h1>
  <p>Everything you need to know before you arrive at Rhizome Springs on Saltspring Island.</p>

  <h2>Getting to Salt Spring Island</h2>

  <h3>By Ferry</h3>
  <p>Ferry reservation is highly recommended if travelling from Vancouver by car.</p>

  <h4>Option 1 — Direct from Tsawwassen</h4>
  <p>Tsawwassen terminal (mainland) direct to Long Harbour terminal (Salt Spring Island). May stop at other Gulf Islands along the way.</p>
  <p><a href="https://www.bcferries.com/routes-fares/schedules/seasonal/PLH-TSA?departureDateCode=R9_20260625_20260907" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BC Ferries: Tsawwassen → Long Harbour schedules</a></p>

  <h4>Option 2 — Via Vancouver Island</h4>
  <p>Take the Tsawwassen → Swartz Bay ferry, then transfer to the Swartz Bay → Fulford Harbour ferry.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.bcferries.com/routes-fares/schedules/seasonal/TSA-SWB?departureDate=20260611-20260907" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tsawwassen → Swartz Bay schedules</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.bcferries.com/routes-fares/schedules/seasonal/SWB-FUL" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Swartz Bay → Fulford Harbour schedules</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>By Floatplane</h3>
  <p>Direct flights from Vancouver (YVR South Terminal or Vancouver Harbour):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://harbourair.com/locations/salt-spring-ganges/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Harbour Air</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.seairseaplanes.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sea Air Seaplanes</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Getting to Rhizome Springs</h2>

  <h3>Transportation on Salt Spring Island</h3>
  <p>There is a <a href="https://www.bctransit.com/salt-spring-island/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">bus service on main roads</a>, but it does not run up Musgrave Road to Rhizome Springs. There is no Uber on Salt Spring Island. <a href="https://saltspringtaxi.ca/taxi-service/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Salt Spring Taxi</a>: 250-537-3030.</p>
  <p>We'll organize a <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1B14DIitf79Ev5g_3GXc0elf8Igc_NahBZLceMEJOrDQ/edit?gid=0#gid=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rideshare spreadsheet</a> so participants can carpool from the ferry terminals.</p>

  <h3>Driving Directions</h3>
  <p>We're located about 25 minutes from Fulford Ferry terminal and 40 minutes from Ganges (the closest stores). The property road is a logging road passable by regular cars at slow speed.</p>
  <p><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/NhkT5cTA5zzbarpQ9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Maps: Rhizome Springs</a></p>

  <div class="notice">
    <p><strong>Step-by-step:</strong> Head south on Musgrave Road to the very south of Salt Spring Island. When the road turns to gravel, check your odometer — we are at the <strong>7 km mark</strong>. Watch for reflectors and "7" spray-painted on a tree. We are the next left after this marker. Look for a <strong>giant cog wheel</strong> at the entrance.</p>
    <p>We neighbour the Kunzang Dechen Osel Ling (KDOL) Retreat Centre. Do <em>not</em> turn onto Mt. Tuam Road — continue down Musgrave Rd approximately 1.5 km past KDOL. When you see the giant white dome, you've arrived.</p>
    <p><strong>Drive at 10 km/hr max</strong> through the neighbour's property. Take a left at the fork and follow the road all the way to the end.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Accommodations</h2>

  <p>General camping is included in the cost of Kin-Fusion Campout. Additional options are available for a separate fee — <strong>book by emailing <a href="mailto:info@rhizomesprings.com">info@rhizomesprings.com</a></strong> as early as possible. Accommodations must be paid in full before arrival.</p>
  <p>You can indicate your preference on the <a href="/register/">registration form</a> and we'll connect you.</p>

  <h3>General Camping (included)</h3>
  <p>Tent or car camping. Bring everything you need. Flat parking spots are available; there are no RV hookups. Compost toilets and hot showers are on site.</p>

  <h3>KDOL Buddhist Centre Cabins</h3>
  <p><strong>CAD $75/night</strong> (single) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>CAD $95/night</strong> (2 people, 2 single beds)</p>
  <p>Cabins at the neighbouring Buddhist retreat centre, about a 10-minute walk through serene forest. Includes use of a common-area outhouse, shower, and simple kitchen. Pillow and sheets provided — bring your own blankets, towel, soap, and shampoo.</p>
  <p class="field-help">Please note: no alcohol, cannabis, or other substances on the KDOL property. Please be respectfully quiet (no speakers, no loud voices), as this is an active place of Buddhist study. Do not contact KDOL directly — all bookings go through Rhizome Springs.</p>

  <h3>Pre-Set Tent (on-site)</h3>
  <p><strong>CAD $65/night</strong></p>
  <p>10-person Coleman tents with a bed frame, real mattress, bedding, blankets, pillow, and towel. On-site at Rhizome with access to compost toilets and hot showers. Bring a flashlight.</p>

  <h3>Geodesic Dome</h3>
  <p><strong>CAD $120/night</strong></p>
  <p>15ft geodesic dome with a queen bed, mattress, bedding, towel, and private shower. Wood burning stove available outside of fire-ban months (June–September is typically under fire ban).</p>

  <h2>On Site</h2>

  <h3>The Dance Dome</h3>
  <p>We'll be dancing in a 50' Zome from Phoenix Domes with a smooth plywood floor. No food or open drinks inside (spill-proof containers only). No outdoor shoes in the studio — bare feet, socks, or indoor dance shoes only.</p>

  <h3>Showers</h3>
  <p>Hot showers on site! We're on a well with limited water — please limit showers to 5 minutes and use biodegradable soap only. We make daily trips to the lake or ocean (about 3 km away) — no soap or oils in the lake.</p>

  <h3>Spirit Lake</h3>
  <p>About 3 km away — an incredible oasis with a sensitive ecosystem (bog, carnivorous plants, rare ecology). <strong>No soaps, shampoos, or sunscreen in the lake.</strong> Rinse off at the showers before heading to the lake if in any doubt.</p>

  <h3>Cell Reception &amp; Power</h3>
  <p>Great cell reception on site; no wifi. Solar power is available at "The Hub" for charging small devices. If you need to charge a large battery system, please check with an organizer first. A cell repair store in Ganges sells Canadian SIM cards and data plans.</p>

  <h2>Pets</h2>
  <p>No dogs on the property. There is a kennel near Swartz Bay ferry terminal on Vancouver Island. <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email us</a> if you need more information.</p>

  <h2>What to Bring</h2>

  <h3>Camping Essentials</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Tent, sleeping pad, pillow, tarp</li>
    <li>Flashlight and extra batteries</li>
    <li>Biodegradable soap, towel, swimsuit</li>
    <li>Sturdy shoes for rugged terrain (flip-flops won't cut it)</li>
    <li>Water bottle, battery pack, sunscreen, bug repellent</li>
    <li>Hot water bottle (nights and mornings get chilly)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Food &amp; Drink</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Coffee/tea thermos and water bottle (plates, bowls, and cutlery provided)</li>
    <li>Extra snacks — meals are served 3× daily but the nearest store is 20–35 min away</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Dance</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Layering clothes for cool mornings and evenings</li>
    <li>Socks or indoor dance shoes — <strong>no outdoor shoes in the studio</strong></li>
    <li>Journal and pen</li>
    <li>Fun costumes or sparkles for the evening</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Please avoid strong perfumes and fragrances.</p>

  <h2>Food</h2>
  <p>Simple meals are served at approximately 9:00 am (breakfast), 1:30 pm (lunch), and 6:30 pm (dinner) on September 11, 12, and 13. The menu is mostly vegetarian. If you prefer a high animal-protein diet, bring extra food for yourself. Fruit, coffee, and tea are available between meals.</p>
  <p>We'll cook with your dietary needs in mind based on your registration. If anything changes before you arrive, let us know.</p>
